\section{Parameters: units, ranges and defaults}{
\describe{
\item{\code{responses}}{path; required. stats fit's responses table, with outcomes for cells. A TSV with a header row: the first column is the feature id (unique, any header) and every other column is one sample, named by its header. Every cell is 0, 1, or blank, NA or NaN (any case) for missing, which is omitted from that feature's fit. mzLib refuses any other value (a proportion is not a binary outcome); the refusal names the feature and sample. A 0 is an outcome, not a missing value. Blank lines are skipped.}
\item{\code{design}}{path; required. stats fit's design table. A TSV with a header row and one row per sample: the sample name, matching the responses header exactly (rows are matched by name, in any order), then one column per coefficient, every cell a finite number. Used as written: include an intercept column if you want one. mzLib refuses a design that is not of full column rank over all samples.}
\item{\code{coefficients} (wire \code{--stdin})}{string[]; required; range \code{>= 1 line; each a design column name, none repeated}. The coefficients to report, one design column name per line. The model always fits every design column; the table holds one block of rows per coefficient named here, in this order.}
\item{\code{max_iterations} (wire \code{--max-iterations})}{int; in \strong{iterations}; default absent; range \samp{>= 1 (mzLib's rule; anything else is mzLib's refusal, a usage error)}. The iteratively reweighted least squares iteration limit per feature (LogisticRegression.Fit maxIterations). A feature still changing at the limit is not_converged. Absent, the bridge sends none and mzLib's default applies (100 at d10017ce), and the envelope's max_iterations is null.}
\item{\code{tolerance}}{float; in \strong{relative change in deviance (unitless)}; default absent; range \samp{> 0 (mzLib's rule; anything else is mzLib's refusal, a usage error)}. Convergence rule (LogisticRegression.Fit tolerance): iteration stops when |dev - dev_prev| / (|dev| + 0.1) is below it, R glm's rule. Absent, the bridge sends none and mzLib's default applies (1e-12 at d10017ce, tighter than glm's default epsilon of 1e-8), and the envelope's tolerance is null.}
\item{\code{threads}}{int; in \strong{threads}; default \code{1}; range \code{>= 1, or -1 for every core}. Features fitted at once. The bridge default is 1 (BULK.md); mzLib's own default is -1. Results are identical at any value (mzLib).}
}
}
